  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "InternReadFile",
    "file": "assimp/code/AssetLib/OFF/OFFLoader.cpp",
    "description": "OFFImporter::InternReadFile allocates `numFaces` aiFace elements and initializes `mesh->mNumFaces = numFaces`, but its face parser handles an invalid face-size token (`idx == 0` or `idx > 9`) by unconditionally decrementing the unsigned `mesh->mNumFaces` and continuing without incrementing the separate loop counter `i`. Consequently, malformed face lines are not bounded by the declared face count; enough such lines underflow `mNumFaces` to a huge unsigned value. ScenePreprocessor::ProcessMesh later trusts that count and reads beyond the allocated `mesh->mFaces` array at ScenePreprocessor.cpp:148.",
    "conditions": "An OFF input must declare nonzero vertex and face counts so a faces array is allocated, then provide more invalid face records than the declared `numFaces` before parsing terminates. Each record whose first integer (the face vertex count) is zero or greater than 9 takes the decrement/continue path without advancing `i`; after more than `numFaces` such records, `mesh->mNumFaces` underflows. The PoV is parsed by the OFF importer (with a `1 9 0` count tuple) and supplies malformed/blank face data that repeatedly reaches this path. On return, scene preprocessing iterates the corrupted face count and performs the heap-buffer-overflow read."
  },
